From 1d513947fc07fcaceee93fad426907f8a71bbf10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:59:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): a busy Board no longer re-runs the full
 repair pass every round [daveey]

The replica's feed cursor is a repair input and moves on every change any gateway makes to the board,
so on a busy Board the sync loop re-ran the full repair pass (partition links, divergence, missing
children, placeholder links) nearly every round. laptop-1 default board, 2026-11-02, no local work:
29 rounds in 90 s, 0.21 s thread-CPU per pass; the sync thread (asyncio_0) used 13.5% of a core.

A change that only moved the replica cursor (same replica file, live revision, schema, mode, gateway
and placement) now waits REPLICA_REPAIR_MIN_S (30 s) after the last pass. Local writes, a rebuilt
replica and config changes still repair at once, and the cheap foreign-parent mirror still runs every
changed round, so a finished foreign parent releases its child without delay. The sync loop selects a
board when its deferred pass is due and caps its wait at that time; a round drops a stale deferral
before doing anything, so a failing board can't make the loop spin.

Live Mac replay (copy of the boards, stub Hub): 10 cursor-only rounds 2.13 s -> 0.05 s thread-CPU.
Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_repair_window.py (RED on the old code: 5 passes for 5 remote
changes). test_kanban_sync_idle_round's remote-change step now advances the repair clock past the window.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py              |  79 +++++-
 .../hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_idle_round.py |   5 +-
 .../test_kanban_sync_repair_window.py         | 261 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 336 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_repair_window.py

